node_modules
out
cache
broadcast

# Foundry dependencies, and the two files a modern `forge install` leaves beside
# them. `forge-std` is installed by hand and by CI at a pinned tag rather than
# vendored or tracked as a submodule — see `05-status.md`. Committing either of
# these would quietly turn it into one.
lib
.gitmodules
foundry.lock

# Secrets. The example is the one file in this family that belongs in the repo.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.next
next-env.d.ts
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

.DS_Store

# Throwaway probes. Never a place for anything that must survive.
.scratch
.superpowers

# Per-person tool settings. The shared half of `.claude/` is tracked; the local
# file is one person's permissions and belongs on one person's machine.
.claude/settings.local.json
.vercel
.env*.local

# Design references. Screenshots of other people's sites, kept beside the work
# while it is being matched. They are not assets: nothing on the page loads them,
# `public/` would serve them from our own domain, and they are three megabytes of
# somebody else's art in a public repo.
public/Landing reference/
